Here's a self-contained Python function that removes any column from a pandas DataFrame df0 whose column-wise maximum exceeds 0. The function tries to use the colmaxfilter library if available (it attempts several plausible API names), and falls back to a pandas-based implementation if colmaxfilter isn't installed or its API is unknown.

